  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Architecture**\n\nOkay, I\'m working on the architecture now. Using the blueprint parameter diagram from the user\'s presentation, I\'m forming the application and web system\'s architecture. It\'s becoming clearer how the digital twin and smart agriculture application will integrate.\n\n\n**Analyzing Core Parameters**\n\nI\'ve been drilling down into the core parameters for the digital twin. The **Digital Twin Crop Kernel** is shaping up as the central node. I\'m focusing on defining the six key measurements: plant height, canopy coverage, growth, disease, fruit ripeness, and crop yield. Each has several sub-parameters to consider, and now I\'m evaluating their interconnectedness for more accurate predictions.\n\n\n**Clarifying Application Role**\n\nI\'m now clarifying the application\'s role and purpose, based on the client\'s needs. The application must function both as a live digital twin and a simulator. I\'m focusing on the interactive visualization canvas with animated crops, telemetry dials, time scrubbers, and environmental controls. Additionally, I need to incorporate an AI vision scanner for real-time plant analysis.\n\n\n**Developing the UI Dashboard**\n\nI\'m now deep in developing the 6-parameter real-time analytics dashboard. I\'m focusing on the sub-views using Recharts, setting telemetry thresholds, and integrating anomaly alerts. I\'m also ensuring the digital twin\'s physical-to-virtual sync status is clearly displayed.\n\nI\'m also building out the technical implementation architecture, which involves illustrating the IoT sensor data flow to cloud middleware. The AI computer vision processing and digital twin engine computations are also being clarified, and visualized. Finally, I am putting together the interactive workflow demonstration for presentation.\n\n\n**Structuring the Source**\n\nI\'m structuring the source files to ensure modularity and cleanliness. I\'m defining key interfaces in `/src/types.ts` for Digital Twin parameters, sensor data, field plots, and AI vision results. This includes the parameters needed for both the slide generator and the architectural components. I\'m also preparing sample data in `/src/data/sampleCrop.ts` to aid testing and initial application setup. I\'m going to follow this initial data by implementing `/src/components` and `/src/services` soon.\n\n\n**Outlining App Components**\n\nI\'m now outlining all the app components. I\'m building datasets for sample crops, including wheat, tomatoes, maize, and strawberries, complete with telemetry and preset photos. I\'m also including detailed technical blueprint data, encompassing hardware specs and the AI pipeline. I am also working on the `/src/components` with specific functional components, such as the `Header`, `DigitalTwinCanvas`, `ParameterGrid`, `AiVisionScanner`, and `BlueprintArchitecture` components.\n\n\n**Defining Implementation**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the implementation details. I\'m building `/src/components/PresentationSlidesExport.tsx` to handle Google Slides integration via Google Workspace GSI OAuth. It will have project and team credits. `/src/components/AnalyticsCharts.tsx` is being developed for time-series graphs, and `/src/components/ClientHowItWorks.tsx` is going to guide clients with an interactive story. I\'m also planning the `/server.ts` Express backend with Vite middleware and Google Slides helper, API calls, and checking the Google Workspace skill for the required scopes.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 10
      nanos: 259249479
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
