    response: "I have successfully enabled Cloud SQL for the `unified-correlate-hxctm` project in the `us-west1` region and configured the foundation for the relational database integration.\n\nHere is a summary of the implementation:\n- **Cloud SQL Provisioning**: Provisioned a new developer edition PostgreSQL instance for your project with scale-to-zero capabilities.\n- **Firebase Auth Integration**: Since all Cloud SQL deployments require Firebase Authentication for secured backend endpoints, I configured the Firebase Admin SDK and created a client-side Google OAuth sign-in utility.\n- **ORM Configuration**: Installed and configured `drizzle-orm` and `drizzle-kit` for schema management. The connection pooling is set up using the object method and the database\'s schema definition is mapped in `/src/db/schema.ts`.\n- **Schema Synchronization**: Generated the initial database structure including a `users` table linked to Firebase Auth `uid`s, and successfully migrated these schema updates to the live Cloud SQL instance.\n\nThe dev server has been restarted and is fully ready for relational data queries."
    modified_response: "I have successfully enabled Cloud SQL for the `unified-correlate-hxctm` project in the `us-west1` region and configured the foundation for the relational database integration.\n\nHere is a summary of the implementation:\n- **Cloud SQL Provisioning**: Provisioned a new developer edition PostgreSQL instance for your project with scale-to-zero capabilities.\n- **Firebase Auth Integration**: Since all Cloud SQL deployments require Firebase Authentication for secured backend endpoints, I configured the Firebase Admin SDK and created a client-side Google OAuth sign-in utility.\n- **ORM Configuration**: Installed and configured `drizzle-orm` and `drizzle-kit` for schema management. The connection pooling is set up using the object method and the database\'s schema definition is mapped in `/src/db/schema.ts`.\n- **Schema Synchronization**: Generated the initial database structure including a `users` table linked to Firebase Auth `uid`s, and successfully migrated these schema updates to the live Cloud SQL instance.\n\nThe dev server has been restarted and is fully ready for relational data queries."
