  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Popup Block**\n\nOkay, so I\'ve pinned down the error `auth/cancelled-popup-request`. Turns out, it\'s likely a Firebase popup issue. It seems the popup gets blocked or closed before it can complete, especially in the AI Studio iframe preview environment. So `signInWithPopup` is getting constrained. I need to figure out how to handle the iframe limitations and ensure the user\'s interaction explicitly triggers the popup.\n\n\n**Addressing Popup Block Issue**\n\nOkay, I\'ve confirmed that the Firebase popup typically works in AI Studio, unless blocked. I think a double-click on the login button might be the issue; that can trigger multiple `signInWithPopup` calls. To mitigate this, I\'m adding a `isLoading` state to disable the button after the initial click. I\'ll modify `LoginScreen.tsx` to include an `isGoogleLoading` state and use it to prevent multiple requests.\n\n\n**Considering Popup Block Alternatives**\n\nNow, I\'m thinking about broader solutions. Specifically, browsers may strictly block popups due to the iframe environment. If `signInWithPopup` fails because of iframe restrictions, I need a clear error message. Browsers like Safari or Brave can be particularly strict. Also, I\'m considering best practices: the environment prefers `signInWithPopup`, and I may need to guide users towards `signInWithRedirect` if they insist on it.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 8
      nanos: 97062705
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
