  planner_response {
    response: "I have added a loading state to the Google Sign-In button and improved the error handling to gracefully manage popup cancellations and browser blocks. \n\nThis error (`auth/cancelled-popup-request`) typically happens when:\n1. The sign-in button is clicked multiple times rapidly.\n2. The browser automatically blocks the popup due to strict privacy settings.\n3. The popup is closed manually before the sign-in process completes.\n\nThe button will now correctly show a \"Connecting...\" spinner, prevent multiple rapid clicks, and display a clear, user-friendly message if the popup is blocked or closed. If you continue to see issues on your specific browser, you may need to explicitly allow popups for this site."
    thinking: "**Summarizing Recent Success**\n\nThe build completed successfully! My focus has been on refining the user experience. I\'ve integrated a loading state, and I improved the error messaging to gracefully manage popup-related issues, particularly the `auth/cancelled-popup-request` error, offering specific user guidance.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have added a loading state to the Google Sign-In button and improved the error handling to gracefully manage popup cancellations and browser blocks. \n\nThis error (`auth/cancelled-popup-request`) typically happens when:\n1. The sign-in button is clicked multiple times rapidly.\n2. The browser automatically blocks the popup due to strict privacy settings.\n3. The popup is closed manually before the sign-in process completes.\n\nThe button will now correctly show a \"Connecting...\" spinner, prevent multiple rapid clicks, and display a clear, user-friendly message if the popup is blocked or closed. If you continue to see issues on your specific browser, you may need to explicitly allow popups for this site."
