  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Handling Rate Limits**\n\nI\'ve determined the error stems from an exhausted Gemini API quota, specifically a 429 rate limit. My focus now centers on graceful error handling. Instead of displaying a disruptive front-end error, I intend to implement a solution that catches the 429 and responds in a user-friendly manner. The goal is to ensure the dashboard continues functioning seamlessly, even when encountering rate limitations.\n\n\n**Analyzing Error Resolution**\n\nI\'m now honing in on the error\'s implications. My initial thought was to use fallback data or display an informative message. However, the requirement is to fix the errors, not just mask them. The thrown error is a 429, indicating API quota exhaustion. I am leaning toward using fallback on the backend when the error is a 429. I am wondering if the issue is with `gemini-3.7-flash`, and if I should just use `gemini-2.5-flash` since that one is working in other endpoints.\n\n\n**Investigating Model Choice**\n\nI\'ve just had a breakthrough. The 429 error, which I initially attributed to a general quota limit, seems directly tied to using `gemini-3.7-flash` for the weather task, even though it\'s recommended for basic text tasks. I\'ve re-examined the documentation and realized that certain models, including those with \"image\" extensions, require a paid API key and a call to the `show_aistudio_ui` tool *before* usage, and `gemini-3.7-flash` is *not* on that list. I will see if switching to a different model fixes this.\n\n\n**Implementing Fallback Logic**\n\nMy focus has shifted to implementing the fallback mechanism. I\'m modifying `server.ts` to check specifically for the 429 status and include `isQuotaExhausted` in the response. This indicator will allow the front-end, within `MainDashboard.tsx`, to handle the error gracefully by displaying fallback weather data and logging a console warning. I think this approach provides a seamless user experience.\n\n\n**Refining Error Display**\n\nI\'ve decided against mock data as per the rule: OAuth or API integration only. Now, I\'m adjusting the UI. I\'ll display a message, \"Weather unavailable (API Quota Exhausted),\" when the quota is exceeded. I\'m updating `MainDashboard.tsx` to handle the `isQuotaExhausted` flag I added previously, and catch `429` errors in the `res.status`. This should provide a good user experience. I\'ve realized though that `res.status === 429` isn\'t currently being sent from the backend, because it\'s returning `500` for all errors, so that will need to be changed in `server.ts`.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_2776567"
      name: "edit_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"Instruction\":\"Pass 429 status correctly back to the frontend\", \"ReplacementContent\":\"      const responseText = response.text || \\\"{}\\\";\\n      const weatherData = JSON.parse(responseText);\\n\\n      return res.json({\\n        success: true,\\n        weather: weatherData,\\n      });\\n    } catch (err: any) {\\n      console.error(\\\"Error in /api/weather:\\\", err);\\n      \\n      const isQuotaError = err?.status === 429 || String(err).includes(\\\"429\\\") || String(err).includes(\\\"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\\\");\\n      \\n      if (isQuotaError) {\\n        return res.status(429).json({\\n          error: \\\"Gemini API Quota Exhausted. Please check your plan.\\\",\\n          isQuotaExhausted: true\\n        });\\n      }\\n\\n      return res.status(500).json({\\n        error: \\\"Failed to fetch weather data using Gemini AI.\\\",\\n        details: err?.message || String(err),\\n      });\\n    }\\n  });\\n\\n  // Vite middleware in dev mode vs static serve in prod\", \"TargetContent\":\"      const responseText = response.text || \\\"{}\\\";\\n      const weatherData = JSON.parse(responseText);\\n\\n      return res.json({\\n        success: true,\\n        weather: weatherData,\\n      });\\n    } catch (err: any) {\\n      console.error(\\\"Error in /api/weather:\\\", err);\\n      return res.status(500).json({\\n        error: \\\"Failed to fetch weather data using Gemini AI.\\\",\\n        details: err?.message || String(err),\\n      });\\n    }\\n  });\\n\\n  // Vite middleware in dev mode vs static serve in prod\", \"TargetFile\":\"/server.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Updating error handling in server\", \"toolSummary\":\"Handle 429 quota error\"}"
