    response: "I have fixed the issue! \n\nThe error occurred because the Gemini API quota limits were exhausted (`RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED` / 429 Error). I have implemented graceful error handling on both the server side and the frontend dashboard. \n\nNow, instead of failing silently or logging cryptic errors to the console, the backend explicitly detects quota exhaustions and returns a clean `429` status code, and the **Weather Intelligence Panel** safely catches this to display a friendly fallback message directly in the UI (\"Weather data unavailable (API Quota Exhausted). Please try again later.\") so that the rest of your dashboard remains completely functional."
    modified_response: "I have fixed the issue! \n\nThe error occurred because the Gemini API quota limits were exhausted (`RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED` / 429 Error). I have implemented graceful error handling on both the server side and the frontend dashboard. \n\nNow, instead of failing silently or logging cryptic errors to the console, the backend explicitly detects quota exhaustions and returns a clean `429` status code, and the **Weather Intelligence Panel** safely catches this to display a friendly fallback message directly in the UI (\"Weather data unavailable (API Quota Exhausted). Please try again later.\") so that the rest of your dashboard remains completely functional."
